# LOCKED — the stage-lock marker

# HOW STAGE COLORS WORK (the "You Are Here" model): a stage's grid color IS its lock state.
#   GREEN = done   — the stage folder contains a file literally named `LOCKED`
#   AMBER = active — the stage named in the analysis's ACTIVE_STAGE file (the ONE room you're in)
#   RED   = open   — everything else (not locked, not active)
#
# TO CLOSE A STAGE: drop a file named `LOCKED` into that stage folder
#   e.g.  echo "closed 2026-01-15: joint sign-off" > analyses/<slug>/stages/02_assignment/LOCKED
#   → the cell turns green.
#
# TO REOPEN A STAGE for more work ("surgery"): delete its LOCKED file
#   → the cell leaves green; if it's also your ACTIVE_STAGE it reads amber ("You Are Here").
#
# THE RULE: to WORK a stage you UNLOCK it. To MOVE ON, LOCK the room you're leaving and point
# ACTIVE_STAGE at the next. Only ever ONE amber (active) stage at a time. Sign-off (S_signoff) is just
# the last stage — locking it means the whole analysis is done.
#
# This file is a `.example` so it does NOT itself lock anything. Copy it to a bare `LOCKED` (any content,
# or empty) inside a stage folder when you close that stage.
